<main class="main-content article-main" id="main-content"><div class="article-shell references-shell">
  <div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Reference library</span></div>
  <header class="page-masthead reveal"><div class="masthead-copy"><span class="article-eyebrow"><span class="kicker-line"></span> FURTHER READING / TRUSTED STARTING POINTS</span><h1>Follow the facts<br><em>further uphill.</em></h1><p class="article-deck">This atlas is an introduction, not the final word. These scientific and public-interest resources can help you verify facts, explore research and learn from conservation work.</p></div><div class="masthead-art"><img src="<%= imageSrc('references.svg') %>" data-image-fallback="/img/references.svg" alt="Illustrated mountains with a reading and research theme"><span>READ / VERIFY / DISCOVER</span></div></header>
  <div class="reference-note reveal"><span>↗</span><p>Use regional scientific literature and protected-area sources when checking the range of a species, current conservation status, official trail conditions or local rules. Those details can change and vary from one mountain region to another.</p></div>
  <section class="reference-grid"><a class="reference-card reveal" href="https://whc.unesco.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><div class="reference-icon">UN</div><span class="small-label">WORLD HERITAGE</span><h2>UNESCO World Heritage Centre</h2><p>Background on protected natural sites, outstanding universal value and selected mountain landscapes.</p><span class="inline-arrow">Visit resource ↗</span></a><a class="reference-card reveal" href="https://www.iucnredlist.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><div class="reference-icon">IUCN</div><span class="small-label">SPECIES & HABITATS</span><h2>IUCN Red List of Threatened Species</h2><p>Consult species assessments, distribution summaries, threats and conservation information.</p><span class="inline-arrow">Visit resource ↗</span></a><a class="reference-card reveal" href="https://www.nps.gov/subjects/geology/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><div class="reference-icon">NPS</div><span class="small-label">EARTH SCIENCE</span><h2>U.S. National Park Service — Geology</h2><p>Accessible explanations of geological processes and landscapes across national parks.</p><span class="inline-arrow">Visit resource ↗</span></a><a class="reference-card reveal" href="https://www.mountainpartnership.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><div class="reference-icon">FAO</div><span class="small-label">PEOPLE & SUSTAINABILITY</span><h2>Mountain Partnership</h2><p>International work on sustainable development, resilient communities and mountain ecosystems.</p><span class="inline-arrow">Visit resource ↗</span></a><a class="reference-card reveal" href="https://www.fao.org/mountain-partnership/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><div class="reference-icon">↗</div><span class="small-label">GLOBAL CONTEXT</span><h2>FAO mountain resources</h2><p>Resources about mountain livelihoods, food systems, resilience and sustainable development.</p><span class="inline-arrow">Visit resource ↗</span></a><a class="reference-card reveal" href="https://www.gmba.unibe.ch/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><div class="reference-icon">GMBA</div><span class="small-label">MOUNTAIN RESEARCH</span><h2>Global Mountain Biodiversity Assessment</h2><p>Research and synthesis about mountain biodiversity patterns, drivers and conservation.</p><span class="inline-arrow">Visit resource ↗</span></a></section>
  <section class="reference-reading reveal"><div><span class="section-index">HOW TO USE SOURCES</span><h2>Read critically.<br><em>Connect the evidence.</em></h2></div><div class="prose"><p>Prefer primary scientific studies, regional field guides, government geological surveys, official park agencies and established conservation assessments. Check publication dates and methods, and distinguish between observed facts, model projections and interpretation.</p><p>Common names can refer to different species, and some mountain ranges span several countries. Confirm the scientific name and geographic scope before applying a claim to an entire range.</p></div></section>
